Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash)

The M = 8 K-quant tensor-op kernel in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_m8_nax.h (compiled into
paged_attn.metallib by crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_m8_nax.metal)
and its host-side K split rule in crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kquant_metal.cpp
(qmm_m8_nax_splits) are ported from Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged_tile.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/split_reduce.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/gguf_linear.metal (the staged decode tile) and
runtime/ops/LinearGguf.cpp (decodeSplits), with the per-format dequantization
rewritten for mlx-node's weight layout; its Q2_K decode (Codes<Q2K>,
bytes8<Q2K> and the CoefCursor Q2K arm) and the QuantKind notion of
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_mode.h (KQ_LINEAR / KQ_CODEBOOK /
KQ_INT8 / KQ_GRID) follow Splash's FmtQ2K, quant_spread2 and QuantKind in
runtime/metal/kernels/common/quant_formats.h. The IQ1_S / IQ1_M / IQ2_XXS /
IQ2_XS / IQ2_S / IQ3_XXS / IQ3_S grid decode in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_grid.h (and its C++ twin in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kquant.cpp) — the 7-bit sign index expansion
(kq_signs7), the per-chunk grid index / sign / scale extraction (IQ3_S's
two 9th index bits per chunk and per-element sign bits), the IQ1
"code - 9" delta form and the power-of-two scale shift — follows Splash's
FmtIQ2XXS, FmtIQ2XS, FmtIQ2S, FmtIQ3XXS, FmtIQ3S, FmtIQ1S, FmtIQ1M,
quant_signs7, quant_iq1_codes and the QuantGrid arm of dequant32 in
runtime/metal/kernels/common/quant_formats.h and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged.h, with the byte fetch rewritten for
mlx-node's three-array layout. The tensor-op verify attention kernel
in crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/segmented_sdpa/sdpa_segmented_nax.metal follows
the matmul2d operand shapes and the page softmax of Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_attention_tile.h, with the segmented
(prefix / new) K/V addressing, causal limits and partial-tile handling
written for mlx-node's two-pass layout. The DFlash2 commit structure — the
packed per-layer GDN state blobs with current/next parity
(crates/mlx-core/src/models/qwen3_5/gdn_blob.rs), the all-layer GDN commit
kernel with the conv carry folded in
(crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/gdn_commit.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_gdn_commit.cpp) and the one-dispatch KV row store
(crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/kv_store_rows.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kv_store.cpp) — follows Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/gdn.metal (verify_gdn_commit, gdn_conv_carry),
runtime/ops/GDN.cpp, runtime/ops/StateLayout.hpp and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_store_row.h, with the arithmetic kept
as mlx-node's per-token bf16 replay and the flat (non-paged) cache layout.
The fused GDN step (crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/gdn_fused_step.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_gdn_fused.cpp) — one threadgroup per value head
running the window's recurrence, then the gated RMSNorm and z gate on the
rows kept in threadgroup memory, writing the window-final state into the
next-parity blob so a full accept is a parity swap (gdn_commit_phase's
early return) — follows the structure of Splash's verify_gdn_fused
(gdn_decode_scan, gdn_decode_gate) in runtime/metal/kernels/decode/gdn.metal
and runtime/ops/GDN.cpp, with the arithmetic kept as MLX's rms_norm kernel
and compiled sigmoid gate so the result equals mlx-node's unfused chain.
